    "content": "Siena, Italy is a historic city in the Tuscany region of central Italy, located roughly 30 miles (48 km) south of Florence. Renowned for its medieval architecture, the Piazza del Campo, and the Siena Cathedral, it is a popular destination set among Tuscan hills. Key Details About Siena, Italy: Location: Central Italy, specifically in the Tuscany region. Geography: Built on three hills and surrounded by a 7-kilometer fortified wall. Geography: It is about 43 miles (70 km) south of Florence and 143 miles (230 km) north of Rome. Surroundings: Located in the heart of the Tuscan countryside, surrounded by vineyards and olive groves. Key Landmarks: Piazza del Campo (site of the Palio horse race), Palazzo Pubblico, and the Duomo di Siena. Alternative Locations: Siena College: A college often associated with March Madness is located in Loudonville, New York, near Albany. Sienna, Poland: A village in the Lesser Poland Voivodeship.",
